On Thu, 15 Oct 2026 16:52:51 -0700, Pat Maddox <pat@patmaddox.com> wrote:
>> I recommend the single port, as you suggested. The version coupling
>> through the schema is real, and the fixes are shared. On your go-ahead
>> I will post it as a patch against net-mgmt/signoz as you accepted it.
>
> It should be a separate port. It's possible to run the signoz collector
> over the network. Thus the two packages have no dependency between
> them.

Agreed. The collector is posted as its own port in "[freebsd-ports
PATCH 0/2] net-mgmt/signoz-otel-collector: New port" [1]. Neither
package depends on the other.

- Patch 1 adds net-mgmt/signoz-otel-collector v0.144.14. It uses
  USES=go:modules with the same sonic swap and bf12ab8 patch as
  net-mgmt/signoz. post-patch adds two vendored _freebsd.go copies.
  The athenz one is exactly what net/redpanda-connect already does,
  and the filestatsreceiver one is fixed upstream by
  opentelemetry-collector-contrib PR 45680, in a release the collector
  does not pin yet. It installs the config from upstream's Linux
  install guide and the OpAMP config as samples. Its rc.d script has
  a "migrate" command that creates or upgrades the ClickHouse schema.
- Patch 2 changes net-mgmt/signoz's pkg-descr and pkg-message to
  name the collector's origin, where they said only that it was
  packaged separately. You may prefer to squash it into the signoz
  commit in your tree.

The series applies on top of the signoz v10 patch [2], because the
collector shares its signoz user and group (UID 485). Upstream runs
both services as signoz in its install guide and Foundry units.

Two things worth knowing before you build it:

- The license is AGPLv3, not Apache 2.0.
- By default, as upstream deploys it, SigNoz manages the collector
  over OpAMP. Until SigNoz answers, the collector runs with nop
  receivers and exporters and ingests nothing. Setting
  signoz_otel_collector_manager_config="" runs the local config
  unmanaged, which suits a collector that is not paired with a SigNoz
  instance.

Checked: makesum, extract, patch, and clean portclippy, portfmt, and
portlint. Not checked: the build and plist, which poudriere will
cover, or a run from rc.d.

One thing I noticed in net-mgmt/signoz while doing this: its
GO_BUILDFLAGS sets -ldflags, and go.mk adds "-ldflags '-s'" only when
GO_BUILDFLAGS has no -ldflags. So the signoz binary is not stripped.
I have not changed it. If you want it stripped, the smallest fix is
to add -s inside its -ldflags string.

